---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InquiryForm from '../components/InquiryForm.astro';
import '../styles/services.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Investing & Trading Lessons | Cloud & Capital" description="Approachable investing and beginner trading lessons with Diana Molski. Understand concepts through worked examples, historical charts, and guided practice.">
  <main id="main-content" class="offer-page">
    <section class="offer-shell offer-intro"><p class="offer-eyebrow">Investing &amp; trading education</p><h1>Make the markets<br /><em>make more sense.</em></h1><p class="offer-lede">A chart is information. It is not a permission slip.</p><p class="offer-summary">I’m Diana. I bring a finance background, curiosity about the markets, and plain-language explanations to tailored lessons. We start with what you already know and the question you want to understand.</p><div class="offer-actions"><a class="offer-button" href="#lesson-inquiry">Ask about a lesson →</a><a href="https://cloudandcapital.substack.com">Read Markets &amp; Mimosas</a></div><p class="offer-route">Looking for help with business costs or reporting? <a href="/services">Explore business services →</a></p></section>
    <section class="offer-shell fit-band"><p class="offer-eyebrow">One topic at a time</p><h2>Understanding first.<br />Then a little practice.</h2><p>We can work through investing basics and ETFs, the differences between swing and day trading, or how to read a historical chart and describe a hypothetical setup. Options are a separate topic after the foundations make sense.</p><p>The goal is to help you explain the concept, ask better questions, and practice a method of thinking.</p></section>
    <section class="offer-shell service-row"><div><p class="offer-eyebrow">A tailored introductory lesson</p><h2>Leave with something<br /><em>you can work through.</em></h2></div><div><ul><li>A short preparation questionnaire and one agreed topic.</li><li>A 60–75 minute lesson with worked examples.</li><li>A concise guide and a historical or paper practice task.</li><li>One follow-up question round within seven calendar days.</li></ul><p>We confirm the topic, format, and fixed fee before booking. Custom indicator development and extensive platform setup are separate scopes.</p><p>Lessons teach concepts and practice. They do not provide personal investment recommendations, live trading signals, or promises of profitable results.</p></div></section>
    <section class="offer-shell process-band"><h2>For a first trading lesson</h2><div class="offer-grid"><div><h3>Read the context</h3><p>Identify the timeframe, price, volume, and relevant levels in a historical example.</p></div><div><h3>Describe the idea</h3><p>State what the hypothetical setup assumes, what would invalidate it, and what remains uncertain.</p></div><div><h3>Practice &amp; reflect</h3><p>Work through a paper example and compare the original reasoning with what happened.</p></div></div></section>
    <section id="lesson-inquiry" class="offer-shell contact-band" aria-labelledby="lesson-title"><p class="offer-eyebrow">Let’s start where you are</p><h2 id="lesson-title">What would you like to understand?</h2><p>Tell me the topic and what you’ve explored. No account balances or holdings are needed.</p><InquiryForm kind="learning" /></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
